                <pb facs="0441" n="359" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg359"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/419A.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the American
                        Ambassador.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-11-15"><hi rendition="#italic">November 15,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Regarding the statement of the President of Mexico, transmitted in your telegram
                    of November 14, that the revolutionists are purchasing arms in the United States
                    and his request that steps be taken to prevent it, these have been communicated
                    to the Department of Justice for its action.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hale.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
